{"_type":"post","category":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"cat-engineering"},"author":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"author-priya"},"slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"cut-agent-latency-speculative-tool-calls"},"coverImage":{"_type":"image","_sanityAsset":"image@https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","alt":"Close-up of a circuit board","caption":"Photo · Unsplash"},"_id":"post-speculative","title":"How we cut agent latency by 60% with speculative tool calls","excerpt":"A look under the hood at the scheduling changes that made Quill Agents 2.0 feel instant — and what we learned shipping them.","publishedAt":"2026-11-04T09:00:00Z","readTime":8,"featured":true,"tags":["Agents","Performance","Infrastructure"],"body":[{"_type":"block","_key":"k0","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1","text":"When we shipped the first version of Quill Agents, the biggest complaint wasn't accuracy — it was ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k2","text":"waiting","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k3","text":". Every tool call added a full round-trip, and complex agents spent most of their time idle.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"k4","_type":"internalLink","reference":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-agents2"}},{"_key":"k5","_type":"link","href":"https://example.com/design-doc","newTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k7","text":"This post walks through how we rebuilt the scheduler, the failures we hit, and the numbers that convinced us to ship. If you're new to the project, start with ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k8","text":"our Agents 2.0 announcement","marks":["k4"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k9","text":" or the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ka","text":"scheduler design doc","marks":["k5"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kb","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kc","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kd","text":"The latency problem","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ke","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kf","text":"A typical agent run is a chain: the model proposes a tool call, we execute it, feed the result back, and repeat. We profiled thousands of runs and found that ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kg","text":"68% of total latency","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kh","text":" was spent waiting, not computing.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"pullQuote","_key":"ki","quote":"The fastest tool call is the one you've already started before you needed it.","attribution":"Priya Krishnan"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kj","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kk","text":"Speculative execution","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kl","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"km","text":"The idea is borrowed from CPUs: while the model is still generating, we predict the most likely tool call and start running it with ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kn","text":"scheduler.predict(trace)","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ko","text":". If it's wrong we discard it — cost: ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kp","text":"a little wasted compute","marks":["highlight"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kq","text":", not a stall.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"codeBlock","_key":"kr","language":"ts","code":"// speculatively run the predicted tool call\nconst speculation = scheduler.predict(trace)\nconst pending = runTool(speculation, { cancelable: true })\n\nconst actual = await model.nextToolCall()\nif (actual.matches(speculation)) return pending\npending.cancel()"},{"_type":"block","_key":"ks","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kt","text":"How the predictor decides","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ku","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kv","text":"The predictor looks at three signals, in order of weight:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kw","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kx","text":"Recent tool-call history for this agent","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"ky","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kz","text":"The partial model output so far","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":2},{"_type":"block","_key":"k10","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11","text":"Static hints from the agent definition","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":3},{"_type":"block","_key":"k12","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13","text":"Per-workspace usage patterns","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":3},{"_type":"block","_key":"k14","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k15","text":"A confidence threshold — below it, we don't speculate","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"k16","style":"h4","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17","text":"Safety rules","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"callout","_key":"k18","tone":"warning","title":"Only speculate on safe tools","text":"Calls with side effects — sending email, writing to a database — are never run speculatively. Tools opt in with a read-only flag."},{"_type":"block","_key":"k19","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1a","text":"Measuring the win","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1b","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1c","text":"After two weeks in production across every workspace, the results held up. Compare the before and after medians:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"statComparison","_key":"k1d","beforeValue":"1.8s","beforeLabel":"Median run, before","afterValue":"0.7s","afterLabel":"Median run, after"},{"_type":"table","_key":"k1e","caption":"Latency by agent complexity (p50)","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k1f","cells":["Agent type","Before","After","Change"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k1g","cells":["Single-step","0.6s","0.5s","−17%"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k1h","cells":["5-step research","3.4s","1.5s","−56%"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k1i","cells":["12-step pipeline","9.8s","3.7s","−62%"]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1j","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1k","text":"A note on methodology","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k1l","text":"1","marks":["sup"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k1m","text":": all numbers are measured server-side, excluding network time to the client. Deprecated approach: ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k1n","text":"raising the timeout","marks":["strike-through"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k1o","text":", which only hid the problem.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"image","_sanityAsset":"image@https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1531482615713-2afd69097998?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","alt":"People collaborating around a table","caption":"The Agents team reviewing latency traces.","_key":"k1p"},{"_type":"imageGallery","_key":"k1q","images":[{"_type":"image","_sanityAsset":"image@https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","alt":"Glowing network across the globe","caption":"Global traffic","_key":"k1r"},{"_type":"image","_sanityAsset":"image@https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555949963-ff9fe0c870eb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","alt":"Code on a laptop screen","caption":"The scheduler code","_key":"k1s"},{"_type":"image","_sanityAsset":"image@https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504384308090-c894fdcc538d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","alt":"Developer at a desk","caption":"Late-night profiling","_key":"k1t"}]},{"_type":"videoEmbed","_key":"k1u","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ","caption":"Scheduler walkthrough from our engineering all-hands"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1v","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1w","text":"What we'd do differently","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1x","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1y","text":"If we started over, we'd invest in the prediction model earlier — a smarter predictor is worth more than a faster executor. We're now exploring ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k1z","text":"multi-call speculation","marks":["underline"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k20","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k21","style":"blockquote","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k22","text":"Early numbers look promising; expect a follow-up.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"ctaButton","_key":"k23","label":"Try Quill Agents free","href":"/#pricing","emphasis":"primary"}],"relatedPosts":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-queue","_key":"k24"},{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-evals","_key":"k25"},{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-structured","_key":"k26"}]}
{"_type":"post","category":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"cat-product"},"author":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"author-alex"},"slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"introducing-quill-agents-2"},"coverImage":{"_type":"image","_sanityAsset":"image@https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1485827404703-89b55fcc595e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","alt":"A friendly robot figure","caption":"Photo · Unsplash"},"_id":"post-agents2","title":"Introducing Quill Agents 2.0","excerpt":"Faster, cheaper, and far more reliable. Here's everything new in our biggest release yet.","publishedAt":"2026-11-02T09:00:00Z","readTime":5,"featured":true,"tags":["Launch","Agents"],"body":[{"_type":"block","_key":"k27","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k28","text":"Today we're releasing ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k29","text":"Quill Agents 2.0","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k2a","text":" to every workspace. It's the biggest update since launch, built around three themes: speed, cost, and reliability.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2b","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2c","text":"What's new","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2d","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2e","text":"Speculative tool calls","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k2f","text":" — runs are up to 60% faster.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2g","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2h","text":"Branching and rollback","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k2i","text":" — version any agent like code.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2j","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2k","text":"Built-in evals","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k2l","text":" — score every run automatically.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2m","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2n","text":"Quality, cost, and latency in one view","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":2},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2o","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2p","text":"Alerts when a score regresses","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":2},{"_type":"callout","_key":"k2q","tone":"tip","title":"Upgrading","text":"Existing agents upgrade automatically. No changes are needed, and you can opt out per agent in Settings."},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2r","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2s","text":"Pricing at a glance","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"k2t","caption":null,"hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k2u","cells":["Plan","Agent runs / month","Evals"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k2v","cells":["Free","1,000","Basic"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k2w","cells":["Team","50,000","Full"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k2x","cells":["Enterprise","Custom","Full + SSO"]}]},{"_type":"ctaButton","_key":"k2y","label":"See pricing","href":"/#pricing","emphasis":"primary"},{"_type":"ctaButton","_key":"k2z","label":"Book a demo","href":"/#faq","emphasis":"secondary"}],"relatedPosts":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-speculative","_key":"k30"},{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-guardrails","_key":"k31"}]}
{"_type":"post","category":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"cat-research"},"author":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"author-dana"},"slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"evaluating-agents-without-ground-truth"},"coverImage":{"_type":"image","_sanityAsset":"image@https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","alt":"Streams of green code on a dark screen","caption":"Photo · Unsplash"},"_id":"post-evals","title":"Evaluating agents without a ground truth","excerpt":"How we score open-ended agent runs when there's no single correct answer.","publishedAt":"2026-10-29T09:00:00Z","readTime":11,"featured":true,"tags":["Evals","Research"],"body":[{"_type":"block","_key":"k32","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k33","text":"Most evaluation advice assumes a right answer. Agents rarely have one. A research agent can produce ten defensible summaries — so what do we grade against?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k34","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k35","text":"Pairwise comparison","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k36","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k37","text":"Instead of scoring an output in isolation, we ask a judge model which of two outputs is better, then aggregate with an Elo-style rating. Formally, the expected score of A over B is E","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k38","text":"A","marks":["sup"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k39","text":" = 1 / (1 + 10","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k3a","text":"(R_B − R_A)/400","marks":["sup"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k3b","text":").","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"codeBlock","_key":"k3c","language":"python","code":"def expected(r_a, r_b):\n    return 1 / (1 + 10 ** ((r_b - r_a) / 400))\n\ndef update(r_a, r_b, a_won, k=24):\n    e = expected(r_a, r_b)\n    return r_a + k * ((1 if a_won else 0) - e)"},{"_type":"pullQuote","_key":"k3d","quote":"A noisy judge is fine, as long as the noise is unbiased.","attribution":"Dana Osei"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k3e","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3f","text":"Choosing a judge","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"k3g","caption":"Judge options we tested","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k3h","cells":["Judge","Agreement with humans","Cost per 1k"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k3i","cells":["Small model","71%","$0.40"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k3j","cells":["Large model","88%","$4.10"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k3k","cells":["Ensemble of three","91%","$2.20"]}]},{"_type":"callout","_key":"k3l","tone":"note","title":"Calibrate first","text":"Always measure judge agreement on a small human-labeled set before trusting it at scale."},{"_type":"block","_key":"k3m","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3n","text":"Further reading","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k3p","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"k3o","_type":"internalLink","reference":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-speculative"}}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3q","text":"Our ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k3r","text":"scheduler post","marks":["k3o"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k3s","text":" for the latency side","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"k3u","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"k3t","_type":"link","href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elo_rating_system","newTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3v","text":"The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k3w","text":"Elo rating system","marks":["k3t"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k3x","text":" on Wikipedia","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1}],"relatedPosts":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-speculative","_key":"k3y"},{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-guardrails","_key":"k3z"}]}
{"_type":"post","category":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"cat-engineering"},"author":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"author-priya"},"slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"durable-job-queue-in-postgres"},"coverImage":{"_type":"image","_sanityAsset":"image@https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558494949-ef010cbdcc31?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80","alt":"Rows of servers in a data center","caption":"Photo · Unsplash"},"_id":"post-queue","title":"Building a durable job queue in Postgres","excerpt":"Why we skipped the extra infra and leaned on the database we already trust.","publishedAt":"2026-10-24T09:00:00Z","readTime":7,"featured":false,"tags":["Infrastructure","Postgres"],"body":[{"_type":"block","_key":"k40","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k41","text":"Every team eventually needs a job queue. We looked at the usual suspects and chose ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k42","text":"SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k43","text":" on Postgres.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k44","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k45","text":"The core query","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"codeBlock","_key":"k46","language":"sql","code":"UPDATE jobs\nSET status = 'running', started_at = now()\nWHERE id = (\n  SELECT id FROM jobs\n  WHERE status = 'queued'\n  ORDER BY run_at\n  FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED\n  LIMIT 1\n)\nRETURNING *;"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k47","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k48","text":"Trade-offs","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"k49","caption":null,"hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k4a","cells":["Option","Ops burden","Throughput","Durability"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k4b","cells":["Postgres","Low","~5k jobs/s","Excellent"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k4c","cells":["Redis streams","Medium","~50k jobs/s","Good"]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"k4d","cells":["Dedicated broker","High","~100k jobs/s","Excellent"]}]},{"_type":"callout","_key":"k4e","tone":"tip","title":"Know your ceiling","text":"At ~5k jobs/s you're fine. Past that, revisit the decision rather than tuning forever."},{"_type":"videoEmbed","_key":"k4f","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ","caption":"Walkthrough of the retry and backoff logic"}],"relatedPosts":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-structured","_key":"k4g"},{"_type":"reference","_ref":"post-speculative","_key":"k4h"}]}
